          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "போராடு — pōrāṭu — \"to struggle; to fight for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விவசாயிகள் தங்கள் உரிமைகளுக்காகப் போராடுகிறார்கள். vivacāyikaḷ taṅkaḷ urimaikaḷukkākap pōrāṭukiṟārkaḷ. The farmers are fighting for their rights."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): போராடினேன், pōrāṭiṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "X-க்காகப் போராடு (pōrāṭu), to fight for X. போராட்டம், a struggle or a protest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "போராடு (pōrāṭu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4540 lists Tamil poru, \"to fight\", with pōr-āṭu, \"to fight\", and pōr-āṭṭam, \"struggle\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
